    <statement><p>Calculate the integral, if it converges.  If it diverges, enter
<alert>diverges</alert> for your answer.</p>
<p><m>\int_{-\infty}^{-1}\,{e^{3 x}\over 1 + e^{3 x}}\,dx =</m>
<fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.0161957838579141</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>w = 1 + e^{3 x}</m>, we have 
<me>\int_{-\infty}^{-1}\,{e^{3 x}\over 1 + e^{3 x}}\,dx = 
\lim\limits_{b\to 1^{+}} \int_b^{1 + e^{-3}} {1\over 3}{dw\over w} = 
\lim\limits_{b\to 1^{+}} {1\over 3}(\ln(1 + e^{-3}) - \ln(b)) = 
  {1\over 3}\ln(1 + e^{-3}).</me>



</solution>
